 "_comment": "Material tiers. Every tier makes the same pieces, and the game builds the items and their recipes from this file: see ItemDatabase::LoadTiers. A piece's stats are its tier's power times the piece's factors; its requirement is the tier's level in the piece's skill. 'ids' and 'names' keep the items that existed before tiers under their old ids, so saves, quests and loot tables still find them. Axes and pickaxes are tools rather than gear: carried, not worn, needing the tier's level in Woodcutting or Mining, and each tier works faster by its 'tool_speed'. Three kinds of armour, one for each way of fighting, and each helps only its own: a tier's metal helm, cuirass and greaves carry 'style_bonus' -- Attack and Strength, scaled by the tier's weapon power -- and 'sets' are the two that are not metal, the ranger's hides and the mage's robes, built for every tier by the same loader. A set piece's defence is the tier's armour power times its 'defence', its Ranged or Magic bonus the tier's weapon power times its 'style', and it needs the tier's level in the set's skill. Hides are cut from the tier's own hide, which something has to be killed for; robes from bolts of cloth and the tier's dye, which is brewed from the herb named.",
